  "newline": true,
  "statement_token": "\"Let $A=\\\\{a_1,a_2,\\\\dots,a_n\\\\}$ be a set with $a_1>a_2>\\\\dots>a_n$ and total sum $\\\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i=n^2$. A **perfect extremal Skolem set** is a perfect Skolem set satisfying this extremal equality. **The perfect extremal Skolem set conjecture.** The set $A$ is a perfect extremal Skolem set if and only if the number of even $a_i$'s is even and\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\sum^m_{i=1}a_i\\\\leq m(2n-m)\\n$$\\n\\nfor each $1\\\\leq m\\\\leq n$. This is the extremal special case of the perfect Skolem set conjecture. The source notes that the analogous assertion fails for multisets, but gives no separate resolution for ordinary sets.\"",
  "statement_token_sha256": "f2f44b6f93eab356a4cad1ec1d54b97e8067aeba8591c9bea2bb8383711192d1",
  "statement": "Let $A=\\{a_1,a_2,\\dots,a_n\\}$ be a set with $a_1>a_2>\\dots>a_n$ and total sum $\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i=n^2$. A **perfect extremal Skolem set** is a perfect Skolem set satisfying this extremal equality. **The perfect extremal Skolem set conjecture.** The set $A$ is a perfect extremal Skolem set if and only if the number of even $a_i$'s is even and\n\n$$\n\\sum^m_{i=1}a_i\\leq m(2n-m)\n$$\n\nfor each $1\\leq m\\leq n$. This is the extremal special case of the perfect Skolem set conjecture. The source notes that the analogous assertion fails for multisets, but gives no separate resolution for ordinary sets.",
